lve so how it works is you have one of  these at each wheel of the car and it  actually has software and sensors built  into this and what it's doing is it's  sensing small perturbations from the  road that are moving the wheels and it's  sensing any sort of motion from the  vehicle itself and what it does is it  tries to cancel out that input you've  seen in suspension this is our next  generation products so here we're  actively isolating we're using a lot of  the similar software and controls but  we're actively isolating a seat  this platform is representing what would  be essentially a very rocky ride on the  roads and the seat there is not moving a  key thing for clear motion to figure out  was how effective its technology might  be at mitigating motion sickness to do  that they enlisted a team of Brandeis  University researchers who are  monitoring test subjects in vehicles  with both clear motion technology and  normal suspension I wanted to put the  clear motion technology to the test  myself so I joined Janet Kaplan a  researcher on the Brandeis team for an  unofficial test ride I get in two cars  one with Clear Motion technology and the  other with a normal suspension this was  a blind test  Kaplan did not tell me which car I'd be  traveling in prior to the ride how do  you feel comfortable or not comfortable  zero read the passage it's a three  minute read I'm reading something about  dream house how clearly were you able to  understand the text on  zero to ten scale three how would you  rate your nausea zero so this vehicle  seemed like this is the active safety I  told you as much yes it is so we're in  car number two we're gonna do it all  again  so press GO are we going on the same  road is before or is this a is this a  rougher road it's the same exactly now  you have to read the text  how nauseous did you feel well I'm  definitely aware that I have a stomach  okay what about understanding the text  tough go probably about a four I just  kind of feel like I'm moving around a  lot definitely wouldn't want to read a  lot we are done we can go back to the  base  Brandeis researchers tested dozens of  subjects for this project and found the  system helped delay and mitigate  symptoms but it's still early days over  who might implement the best  countermeasure for motion sickness clear  motion faces competition from tech and  auto giants after taking two cars on two  different test rides I can tell you that  I could tell the difference between  these vehicles the ride in the second  vehicle was a lot rougher a lot less of  an enjoyable experience it was difficult  to pay attention to the reading material  and I can imagine a situation if this  was an autonomous car and I had all the  time in the world to be reading I  wouldn't want to be doing it and which  underscores really why this company and  others are trying to develop technology  to combat motion sickness so one of the  challenges in this sector is that some  only some automakers and some tech  companies were very enthusiastic about  the deployment of fully autonomous  vehicles since then we've seen kind of  pull back in some of these timelines how  does that affect you as you try to  supply them for the parts they need in  the future  yeah so that's that's one of the keys  we've got a product that meets a need  today which is better ride  and safety and then you have this sort  of longer-term story so for us the  potential push out of autonomy is not a  huge factor because all of our contracts  today are really around you know  supplying to vehicles that are being  produced I'd say another thing that's  also interesting is this concept of the  head start I mean people are finally  finally recognizing that EVs are going  to be very important and Tesla's  effectively operating this bubble for a  decade they've got a serious head start  from the other automakers  and likewise we see sort of this sort of  Head Start mentality where starting out  in the premium segment we've built a  patent portfolio of 280 patents so far  then we see this sort of head start  let's get out there  prove out the technology as soon as this  market comes and we're gonna be running  clear motion has raised about two  hundred and eighty million dollars to  date with participation from Microsoft  and Bridgestone these kinds of  investments show that investors are  thinking about what needs to occur after  driverless cars or deployed years from  now and what humans are going to need as  passengers  you  [Music]

